<%- include('partials/admin-open', { title: 'Stage admin', user: user, section: 'stage', admIsAdmin: !!(typeof isAdmin !== 'undefined' && isAdmin) }) %>
<%# 1.99ack: the admin-only parts ask their own capability (siteperms.js) %><% const _can = locals.can || new Function(include('../siteperms-core.js'))().viewCan(locals);
   const oaCfg = _can('onair.config'), rsMain = _can('restream.main'), mediaOk = _can('media.admin'); -%>
<!-- views/stageAdmin.ejs — paid Main Stage slots: settings, open slots (cut), bans, booking log. -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/public/css/stage.css?v=9">
<% const C = state.config; %>
<main class="sb" id="sa">
  <div class="sb-head">
    <h1><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📺</span> Stage admin</h1>
    <p class="lede">Pad stages: user slots, featuring, scheduling. RTMP application: <code><%= state.rtmp_app %></code>. <a href="/stage/book">Booking page ›</a><% if (mediaOk) { %> · <a href="/admin/media#library">📼 Play from library ›</a><% } %></p>
  </div>

  <section class="sb-card" id="open" aria-labelledby="openT">
    <h2 id="openT">On the stage now</h2>
    <div class="row"><button type="button" class="btn danger" id="cutAll">✂ Cut everything to Pepe</button></div>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>Status</th><th class="num">Live</th><th class="num">Charged / held</th><th>Booked</th><th></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="openRows"></tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <!-- 1.99lm: featuring - Pepe's stream for events, and the automatic feature of a live user stream (takeover_mode) -->
  <section class="sb-card" id="featCard" aria-labelledby="ftT">
    <h2 id="ftT"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">★</span> Featuring</h2>
    <p id="pfNow" role="status">Loading…</p>
    <div class="row">
      <button type="button" class="btn primary" data-pf="on">★ Feature Pepe's stream until I turn it off</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-pf="off">Stop featuring Pepe's stream</button><span class="msg" id="pfMsg" role="status"></span>
    </div>
    <form id="pfForm" class="row" autocomplete="off">
      <label>For <input type="number" name="minutes" min="1" max="43200" placeholder="minutes" style="width:7em" aria-label="Minutes"></label>
      <label>or from <input type="datetime-local" name="from" aria-label="From"></label>
      <label>until <input type="datetime-local" name="until" aria-label="Until"></label>
      <input type="text" name="note" maxlength="80" placeholder="event (optional)" aria-label="Event name">
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Schedule</button>
    </form>
    <p class="muted">While Pepe's stream is featured, no user stream is featured automatically on any pad (one that is up is dropped); owners can still feature a slot by hand. <b>Auto-feature</b> (<i>Settings</i> below, and per pad on its settings page): a stream that goes live on a pad where nothing is featured becomes that pad's featured stream - its stage's default view, the homepage when it's the front pad, Top Pads' now playing, the ★ in the guide and schedule - until it ends; then the next live one (the first to go live), else Pepe's stream. It shows under <i>On the stage now</i> as <b>auto-featured (live)</b>; <b>Cancel auto-feature</b> drops it for that stream for good (another live stream may take over).</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 1.99fv: what Pepe's main stage plays (stage setting pepe_embed; null = his own stream) -->
  <% const PS = state.pepe_src || { mode: 'stream' }; const twCh = PS.twitch && PS.twitch.login; %>
  <section class="sb-card" id="pepeSrc" aria-labelledby="psT">
    <h2 id="psT"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🐸</span> Pepe's main stage source</h2>
    <p id="psNow" role="status"><% if (PS.mode === 'embed') { %>Showing an embed: <b><%= PS.label %></b><% if (PS.url) { %> · <a href="<%= PS.url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><%= PS.url %></a><% } %><% } else { %>Showing <b>Pepe's stream (HLS + ⚡)</b> - the default.<% } %></p>
    <div class="row">
      <button type="button" class="btn primary" data-ps="pepe" <%= PS.mode === 'embed' ? '' : 'disabled' %>>↩ Back to Pepe's stream</button>
      <% if (twCh) { %><button type="button" class="btn" data-ps="twitch">🟣 Twitch embed (twitch.tv/<%= twCh %>)</button><% } %>
    </div>
    <form id="psForm" class="row" autocomplete="off">
      <input type="text" name="pepe_embed" maxlength="300" spellcheck="false" style="flex:1 1 280px" aria-label="Twitch channel or YouTube / Twitch link"
             placeholder="Twitch name or link, or a YouTube video / live link">
      <button type="submit" class="btn">Use this embed</button><span class="msg" id="psMsg" role="status"></span>
    </form>
    <p class="muted">Pepe's stream is the default: lowest delay, ⚡ WebRTC, snaps / clips. Twitch going live never switches it by itself (Twitch is a relay of his stream). An embed takes the same links as a streamer's slot. Either way, ON AIR, snaps / clips and the front-pad pick follow Pepe's own stream; viewers can still pick "Pepe's own stream" next to his tab.</p>
  </section>

  <% if (oaCfg) { %>
  <!-- 1.99yt: 📺 On Pepe's OBS (onair.js POC) - one live slot or cam on his main stream + his Camfrog cam -->
  <section class="sb-card" id="oaCard" aria-labelledby="oaT">
    <h2 id="oaT"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">📺</span> On Pepe's OBS <small class="muted">(POC)</small></h2>
    <p id="oaNow" role="status">Loading…</p>
    <div class="row"><button type="button" class="btn danger" id="oaOff" disabled>⏹ Take it off Pepe's stream</button><span class="msg" id="oaMsg" role="status"></span></div>
    <div id="oaBlocked" class="muted"></div>
    <h3>Live slots</h3>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>Pad</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="oaSlots"></tbody></table></div>
    <h3>Cams</h3>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>Room</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="oaCams"></tbody></table></div>
    <form id="oaCfg" class="settings" autocomplete="off">
      <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="enabled"> On-air enabled <small>(kill switch)</small></label>
      <%# stagefix site (D-9): off excuses only cams their owner shows to everyone - a members cam (the default) still needs its owner's OK, given after they last changed its mode; followers / on-request cams never go on %>
      <label class="chk" title="Off: only cams their owner shows to everyone go on without asking. A members cam (the default) always needs its owner's OK, given after they last changed who may see it; followers and on-request cams never go on."><input type="checkbox" name="cam_optin"> Cams need their owner's opt-in <small>(off: only cams shown to everyone are excused)</small></label>
      <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="allow_library"> Allow 📼 Plex plays <small>(Twitch relay: DMCA risk)</small></label>
      <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="auto_scene"> Switch OBS to the on-air scene when needed</label>
      <label class="chk" title="When the operator's IRL feed goes live while OBS is on one of these scenes, OBS switches to the on-air scene (Pepe) and back when it ends. Needs !onair setup irl once (the IRL source keeps its receiver open while hidden). Not tied to the on-air switch."><input type="checkbox" name="irl_switch"> 🎥 IRL auto-switch</label>
      <label class="chk" title="The pick's sound also goes into Pepe's Camfrog mic (the same cable as Spotify), so rooms with !mic onair on hear it while Pepe holds the mic. Needs !onair setup audio once."><input type="checkbox" name="mic_audio"> 🎤 Pick's sound on Pepe's mic</label>
      <label>&nbsp;↳ from scenes <small>(comma-separated)</small><input type="text" name="irl_from" maxlength="300" spellcheck="false" placeholder="BRB, Gaming"></label>
      <details class="adm-adv" style="grid-column: 1 / -1"><summary>OBS names and the cam encode</summary><div class="adm-adv-body settings">
        <label>Switch OBS to this scene (on-air + IRL) <small>(one that shows the IRL scene with nothing big over it)</small><input type="text" name="scene" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false"></label>
        <label>IRL scene (nested)<input type="text" name="irl_scene" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false"></label>
        <label>IRL feed source (wins)<input type="text" name="irl_source" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false"></label>
        <label>On-air source<input type="text" name="source" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false"></label>
        <label>On-air browser source (embeds)<input type="text" name="web_source" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false"></label>
        <label>Embed not playing → off after (s)<input type="number" name="embed_stall_s" min="30" max="600"></label>
        <label>Owner's OK expires after (min)<input type="number" name="consent_min" min="1" max="60"></label>
        <label>Cam fps<input type="number" name="cam_fps" min="5" max="30"></label>
        <label>Cam kbps<input type="number" name="cam_kbps" min="200" max="6000"></label>
      </div></details>
      <!-- 1.99acw: 🖼 pictures / 🔗 cards / 🌐 live pages (onairmedia.js) -->
      <fieldset class="adm-adv" style="grid-column: 1 / -1" id="oaMediaFs"><legend>🖼 Pictures &amp; links</legend><div class="settings">
        <label class="chk" title="Staff can put pictures (safety-checked, served from publicaccess.tv), link cards and - with the switch below - live pages on Pepe's stream. Needs the kill switch on and !onair setup media once."><input type="checkbox" name="media_enabled"> 🖼 Pictures &amp; links on air <small>(onair_media)</small></label>
        <label class="chk" title="A live page is the real page in Pepe's OBS - his VM loads it, so the site sees his home internet address. Off by default everywhere. Pepe also refuses live pages until his VM's firewall attestation (onair_live_firewall), his admin panel login and an OBS websocket password are in place - his own address check covers only the first hop (the page can redirect or frame anything after it), the VM firewall is what keeps it off the home network. Staff only (locked)."><input type="checkbox" name="live_pages"> 🌐 Live pages <small>(staff; Pepe's VM loads them; needs his VM firewall step)</small></label>
        <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="overlay_over_irl"> Corner items stay up over the IRL feed</label>
        <label>Picture / card: default (s)<input type="number" name="media_secs" min="5" max="600"></label>
        <label>Picture / card: at most (s)<input type="number" name="media_max_s" min="10" max="600"></label>
        <label>Live page: default (s)<input type="number" name="live_secs" min="10" max="600"></label>
        <label>Live page: at most (s)<input type="number" name="live_max_s" min="10" max="600"></label>
        <label>Direct (unscanned) picture: at most (s)<input type="number" name="direct_max_s" min="10" max="300"></label>
        <label>Corner box (% of the width)<input type="number" name="corner_pct" min="15" max="50"></label>
        <label>Picture size cap (MB)<input type="number" name="max_image_mb" min="1" max="15"></label>
        <label>Per person per 10 min<input type="number" name="media_per_10min" min="1" max="60"></label>
        <label>Live pages may never open <small>(hosts, comma-separated; the site's own are always refused)</small><input type="text" name="live_deny" maxlength="600" spellcheck="false" placeholder="example.com, other.example"></label>
        <label>Program scenes that get the corner scene<input type="text" name="top_scenes" maxlength="300" spellcheck="false"></label>
        <label>Corner scene (nested)<input type="text" name="top_scene" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false"></label>
        <label>Corner browser source<input type="text" name="corner_source" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false"></label>
        <label>Live-page browser source<input type="text" name="live_source" maxlength="60" spellcheck="false"></label>
      </div></fieldset>
      <div class="row" style="grid-column: 1 / -1"><button type="submit" class="btn">Save</button><span class="msg" id="oaCfgMsg" role="status"></span></div>
    </form>
    <details><summary class="muted">Log</summary><div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What</th><th>By</th><th>Target</th><th>Detail</th><th>Address</th></tr></thead><tbody id="oaLog"></tbody></table></div></details>
    <p class="muted">Pepe plays the pick in a media source under his IRL feed (OBS scene <i>IRL</i>, which sits in his program scenes under his avatar and overlay), so it goes out on his main stream, the Twitch relay and his Camfrog cam (the virtual camera shows the program scene). The operator's own IRL feed always wins: while it plays, the pick is hidden. YouTube / Twitch embeds play in a second (browser) source - tick “I have the rights to rebroadcast this” each time; one that stops playing (ad, unavailable, offline) is taken off. Approved-only pads and cams whose owner hasn't opted in need the owner's OK: “Ask the owner” sends them an instant request (inbox, Camfrog PM, a prompt on the pad) and it goes on air only after they allow it. Never NSFW slots. A slot's streamer is told and can take it off (<code>!onair off</code>); a cam needs its owner's opt-in (Settings → Privacy, or <code>!onair me on</code>) and Pepe tells them in Camfrog. It ends by itself when the slot ends or the cam goes. Camfrog: <code>!onair &lt;pad|user|slot id&gt;</code>, <code>!onair cam &lt;login&gt;</code>, <code>!onair off</code> (admins).
      🖼 Pictures and 🔗 link cards (staff, the player bar's Image / Link tabs or <code>!onair image|link &lt;link&gt; … rights</code>) are fetched by the site, re-encoded and safety-checked (anything not clearly safe is refused), and shown from publicaccess.tv - full screen or in a corner, for a set time. Direct pictures (unscanned) and 🌐 live pages are Staff and up only (locked) and make Pepe's OBS load the address itself - Pepe offers them only after his VM firewall step (his own address check is a first-hop check only). <code>!onair off corner</code> clears only the corner; <code>!onair off [corner] block</code> or ⛔ on the player bar also blocks what was shown (deleted, never again). Three unsafe refusals in 24 h (or a possible-minor flag) block that person's pictures &amp; links - lift it above.</p>
  </section>
  <% } %>

  <!-- 1.99fk: 🟣 Twitch relays (restream.js) -->
  <section class="sb-card" id="rsCard" data-mode="admin" aria-labelledby="rsT">
    <h2 id="rsT"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🟣</span> Twitch relays</h2>
    <p id="rsWorker" class="muted">Loading…</p>
    <h3>Pepe's main stream</h3>
    <div id="rsMain"></div>
    <% if (rsMain) { %>
    <details class="adm-adv"><summary>Set / replace Pepe's Twitch key</summary>
      <form id="rsForm" class="settings" autocomplete="off">
        <label>Twitch stream key<input type="password" name="key" autocomplete="new-password" spellcheck="false" maxlength="200" placeholder="live_…"></label>
        <label>Ingest server <span class="muted">(optional)</span><input type="text" name="server" spellcheck="false" maxlength="200" placeholder="auto (rtmp://live.twitch.tv/app)"></label>
        <div class="row" style="grid-column: 1 / -1"><button type="submit" class="btn primary">Save</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn danger hide" data-rs-del>Delete key</button><span class="msg" id="rsMsg" role="status"></span></div>
      </form>
    </details>
    <% } %>
    <h3>Streamers</h3>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>Key</th><th>Relay</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="rsRows"></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="muted">A relay runs only while the stream is live, its switch is on and a key is saved; it copies the stream (no re-encode). Admins can switch any relay off. Emergency stop of every relay: <code>systemctl stop patv-restream@prod</code> on the VPS.</p>
  </section>

  <% if (typeof mf !== 'undefined' && mf) { %>
  <!-- micfollow: 🎙 mic follows on the pads' own stages (micfollow.js). Staff (micfollow.kill): the kill switch + turning it off
       on one pad. Admins (micfollow.admin): the knobs + the appearance log. Client: public/js/stage-mf-admin.js -->
  <section class="sb-card" id="mfCard" aria-labelledby="mfT">
    <h2 id="mfT"><span class="ds-ic" aria-hidden="true">🎙</span> Mic follows</h2>
    <p class="muted">In a pad whose owner turned it on, whoever holds the Camfrog mic shows on <b>that pad's</b> stage with their cam (several at once in a layout drawn by the browser). Only people Pepe can prove are who they say, only to the pad's signed-in members, never on Pepe's stream, Twitch, the homepage or any public page. Opt-outs (the website switch, <code>!livecam off</code>, the new "mic stage" switch, cam access set to followers / on request, private activity, <code>!bridge hide</code>) cut within about 2 s.</p>
    <div class="row"><label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" id="mfKill"<%= mf.cfg.enabled ? ' checked' : '' %>> <b>Mic follows on</b> (site-wide kill switch)</label>
      <input type="text" id="mfKillWhy" placeholder="reason (optional)" aria-label="Reason" maxlength="200"><span class="msg" id="mfKillMsg" role="status"></span></div>
    <h3>Pads using it</h3>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Pad</th><th>Layout</th><th class="num">On stage</th><th class="num">Live</th><th class="num">Stills</th><th>Status</th><th title="Pepe's last complete read of the room's people list, failed opens / stills in the last hour, and the cards shown now">Health</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="mfPads"></tbody></table></div>
    <h3>⚑ Reports to review</h3>
    <p class="muted">Viewers report a tile with ⚑ (it hides for them at once). Two qualified reporters within a couple of minutes take the person off that pad's mic stage for a day, pending your review. <b>Dismiss</b> lifts it (those reporters don't count against that person for 24 h); <b>Uphold</b> keeps it.</p>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Pad</th><th>Camfrog login</th><th class="num">Reports</th><th class="num">Qualified</th><th>Why</th><th>Last</th><th>Status</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="mfReports"></tbody></table></div>
    <h3>Last 24 hours</h3>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><tbody id="mfMetrics"></tbody></table></div>
    <% if (mf.admin) { %>
    <details class="adm-adv"><summary>Settings (admins)</summary>
      <form id="mfCfg" class="settings"><div class="row" style="grid-column: 1 / -1"><button type="submit" class="btn primary">Save mic follows settings</button>
        <input type="text" name="reason" placeholder="reason (optional)" aria-label="Reason" maxlength="200"><span class="msg" id="mfCfgMsg" role="status"></span></div></form>
    </details>
    <details class="adm-adv"><summary>Appearance log (admins, 30 days)</summary>
      <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Started</th><th>Pad</th><th>Login</th><th class="num">On stage (s)</th><th class="num">With video (s)</th><th class="num">Peak viewers</th><th>Ended because</th></tr></thead><tbody id="mfSpans"></tbody></table></div>
    </details>
    <% } %>
  </section>
  <script id="mfState" type="application/json"><%- JSON.stringify(mf).replace(/</g, '\\u003c') %></script>
  <script src="/public/js/stage-mf-admin.js?v=3" defer></script>
  <% } %>

  <section class="sb-card" id="settings" aria-labelledby="setT">
    <h2 id="setT">Settings</h2>
    <form id="cfg" class="settings">
      <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" <%= C.enabled ? 'checked' : '' %>> Booking open</label>
      <label title="1.99lm: a user stream that goes live on a pad where nothing is featured becomes its featured stream until it ends. Pads can override this on their settings page.">★ Auto-feature live streams<select name="takeover_mode">
        <option value="when_idle" <%= C.takeover_mode !== 'off' ? 'selected' : '' %>>When nothing is featured (default)</option>
        <option value="off" <%= C.takeover_mode === 'off' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Off</option></select></label>
      <label>Max slot price (PAT / live minute)<input type="number" name="price_per_min" min="1" value="<%= C.price_per_min %>"></label>
      <label>Min minutes<input type="number" name="min_minutes" min="1" value="<%= C.min_minutes %>"></label>
      <label>Max minutes <small>(a pad's default)</small><input type="number" name="max_minutes" min="1" max="360" value="<%= C.max_minutes %>"></label>
      <label>Longest a pad owner may allow <small>(minutes, up to 360 = 6 h; also a 📼 Plex slot's limit)</small><input type="number" name="pad_max_minutes" min="5" max="360" value="<%= C.pad_max_minutes %>"></label>
      <label>User streams at once, site-wide<input type="number" name="max_concurrent" min="0" max="32" value="<%= C.max_concurrent %>"></label>
      <label>Most slots an owner can give a pad<input type="number" name="max_slots_per_room" min="1" max="8" value="<%= C.max_slots_per_room %>"></label>
      <label>Book ahead up to (days)<input type="number" name="schedule_days" min="0" max="60" value="<%= C.schedule_days %>"></label>
      <label>Upcoming bookings per user<input type="number" name="schedule_per_user" min="0" max="20" value="<%= C.schedule_per_user %>"></label>
      <details class="adm-adv" style="grid-column: 1 / -1"><summary>Advanced: scheduling, queue and timing</summary><div class="adm-adv-body settings">
      <label>Key works before start (min)<input type="number" name="lead_min" min="0" max="30" value="<%= C.lead_min %>"></label>
      <label>Queue length per pad<input type="number" name="queue_max" min="0" max="50" value="<%= C.queue_max %>"></label>
      <label>Go-live window (min)<input type="number" name="start_window_min" min="1" value="<%= C.start_window_min %>"></label>
      <label>Off-air grace (min)<input type="number" name="idle_grace_min" min="1" value="<%= C.idle_grace_min %>"></label>
      <label>Bookings / user / hour<input type="number" name="bookings_per_hour" min="1" value="<%= C.bookings_per_hour %>"></label>
      </div></details>
      <label class="chk" title="Kill switch: off hides 📸 Snap / 🎬 Clip on every stage player, and the site and Pepe refuse saves"><input type="checkbox" name="stagecap_enabled" <%= C.stagecap_enabled !== false ? 'checked' : '' %>> Viewers can snap / clip the stages</label>
      <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="stagecap_snaps" <%= C.stagecap_snaps !== false ? 'checked' : '' %>> &nbsp;↳ stage snaps</label>
      <label class="chk"><input type="checkbox" name="stagecap_clips" <%= C.stagecap_clips !== false ? 'checked' : '' %>> &nbsp;↳ stage clips</label>
      <label class="chk" title="1.99et: WHIP ingest (OBS 30+ / browser), ⚡ Low latency (WHEP) players, /api/turn. Needs MediaMTX + coturn (deploy/webrtc). Off = no WebRTC anywhere."><input type="checkbox" name="webrtc_enabled" <%= C.webrtc_enabled === true ? 'checked' : '' %>> ⚡ WebRTC ultra-low latency (WHIP / WHEP)</label>
      <label title="1.99il: the pads' Camfrog room audio over WebRTC (~0.5 s behind the room instead of ~1.5 s). Needs ⚡ WebRTC above and a Pepe that publishes it. Anyone it can't reach (no UDP, TURN full, old browser) gets the normal MP3 relay automatically.">⚡ Room audio over WebRTC<select name="room_rtc">
        <option value="off" <%= C.room_rtc !== 'prime' && C.room_rtc !== 'all' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Off (MP3 relay only)</option>
        <option value="prime" <%= C.room_rtc === 'prime' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Prime Time pads (+ comped admin pads)</option>
        <option value="all" <%= C.room_rtc === 'all' ? 'selected' : '' %>>Every pad</option></select></label>
      <label title="1.99il: WebRTC room listeners at once, site-wide (TURN relay capacity is ~40 sessions, shared with the stages' ⚡). Over it, new listeners get the MP3 relay. 0 = none.">⚡ Room audio WebRTC listeners, max<input type="number" name="room_rtc_cap" min="0" max="500" value="<%= C.room_rtc_cap %>"></label>
      <div class="row" style="grid-column: 1 / -1"><button type="submit" class="btn primary">Save settings</button><span class="msg" id="cfgMsg" role="status"></span></div>
    </form>
    <p class="muted">1.99bi: every pad has its own stage. Pad owners set their pad's slot count (up to the cap above) and an optional price for slots (free by default, at most the max above). 1.99ee: featuring can't be bought - the owner features a slot for free, the front page is the automatic ranking, and pads are 🚀 boosted instead. Slot fees and boosts settle as a room flow: half to the Federal Reserve (Fort Knox's stand-in), half held in the pad's room-vault escrow. A slot keeps the price it was booked at. (1.99ep: the bookings from before boosts were cleaned up.) Owners: <a href="/pads/admin">Pads admin ›</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="sb-card" id="bans" aria-labelledby="banT">
    <h2 id="banT">Banned from booking</h2>
    <form id="banForm" class="row"><input type="text" name="username" placeholder="username" required aria-label="Username to ban">
      <input type="text" name="reason" placeholder="reason (optional)" aria-label="Reason"><button type="submit" class="btn danger">Ban</button></form>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>User</th><th>Reason</th><th>By</th><th>When</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="banRows"></tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="sb-card" id="log" aria-labelledby="logT">
    <h2 id="logT">Booking log</h2>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Booked</th><th>Who</th><th class="num">Max</th><th class="num">Live</th><th class="num">Held</th><th class="num">Charged</th><th class="num">Refunded</th><th>Ended</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="logRows"></tbody></table></div>
  </section>

  <section class="sb-card" id="events" aria-labelledby="evT">
    <h2 id="evT">Recent events</h2>
    <div class="tblwrap"><table><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What</th><th>By</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody id="evRows"></tbody></table></div>
  </section>
</main>
<script id="saState" type="application/json"><%- JSON.stringify(state).replace(/</g, '\\u003c') %></script>
<script src="/public/js/stage-admin.js?v=5" defer></script>
<script src="/public/js/restream.js?v=1" defer></script>
<% if (oaCfg) { %><script src="/public/js/onair-admin.js?v=3" defer></script><% } %>
<%- include('partials/admin-close') %>
</body>
</html>
